Source: vmgui-guest
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Maintainer: scroll-secure <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: vmgui-guest
Architecture: all
Depends: waypipe, python3, systemd, ${misc:Depends}
Description: show this VM's windows on the host's scroll session (vmgui)
 Runs waypipe server on a vmgui display in the user session and forwards each
 app over vsock to the host, where vmgui-host draws it framed in the VM's color.
 Also llmctl, which controls the host's model server over vsock.

Package: vmgui-guest-wlroots
Architecture: all
Depends: vmgui-guest (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: vmgui: native Wayland apps default to the vmgui display
 environment.d defaults so Wayland apps use the vmgui display.

Package: vmgui-guest-xorg
Architecture: all
Depends: vmgui-guest (= ${binary:Version}), xwayland-satellite, ${misc:Depends}
Description: vmgui: X11 apps through xwayland-satellite
 xwayland-satellite on the vmgui display as X server :7, so X11 apps show up
 on the host as ordinary windows. Needs a release that packages
 xwayland-satellite (Debian 13 and forky don't yet).
